    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 13th with a primary objective of hunting stolen base volume, making **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.37) and **Caleb Durbin** (66.18) our offensive anchors. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a prime leadoff spot against Cavalli, where his elite speed profile is boosted by a favorable park factor and a solid platoon edge against the right-hander. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** is our top play today; while he faces a veteran in Scherzer, the 5.10 xERA suggests significant vulnerability, and the prospect of facing a pitcher with a slow delivery provides an ideal green light for **Caleb Durbin** to maximize our SB category. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (65.44) as he leverages a dynamic platoon advantage against Roki Sasaki, effectively mitigating the risk of facing a high-level arm.\n\nThe rotation decision for our middle infield was tightly contested, ultimately landing on **Trea Turner** (60.85) over our depth options. **Trea Turner** is priced in due to the high-probability environment for stolen bases against Bradley, despite a wind-in warning that tempers his power ceiling. **Chase Meidroth** (62.45) serves as a high-floor spark plug from the leadoff spot; his 19% boost from the matchup against a 5.02 xERA arm makes him an automatic start. Among those on the outside looking in, **Colt Keith** narrowly missed the final cut; while he held a respectable baseline, his lack of a confirmed spot in the lineup combined with a neutral-to-negative platoon outlook against Messick forced us to relegate him to the bench to preserve our game caps.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our lineup-pending slots, specifically **Gary Sanchez** (48.01) and **Kyle Schwarber** (57.64). **Gary Sanchez** is currently floating at our marginal floor and requires confirmation of his spot in the order to justify the start, as his reliance on power against Roki Sasaki is volatile. Similarly, **Kyle Schwarber** faces a wind-in warning that threatens his high-exit-velocity profile. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Carson Benge** sidelined by scheduling, our roster depth is being pushed to its limits; we will be monitoring the status of **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** closely as potential late-inning replacements should our primary starters fail to clear the 50-point efficiency threshold.",
